{"title":"Normalizer","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>normalizer</b> is a part of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Group\" title=\"Group\">group</a>.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be a subset of a group <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  An element <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is said to <i>normalize</i> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/a/45a5ca10535cecc02a1922c94311dee8dc4e734d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$bAb^{-1} = A$\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />.  A subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is said to normalize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> if all its elements normalize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.  The set of all elements of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> that normalize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is called the <i>normalizer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /></i>.  It is often denoted as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/0/880571c656c3a58ae071d005223cac947e2aa4d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_G(A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/a/86a7dc9448d1984863ede071f249a88b7cde960f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N(A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" />, when there is no risk of confusion.  It is evidently a subgroup of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />; for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/6/bc6cac38fddf33fcce0cc6590733d20151c6e90b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e \\in N(A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" />; if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/d/c9dd1fe4590b39259c898e9d691785862c2ce836.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> normalize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/f/88fd32cdb545ffcef97145bf7f1e280628c45d4b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(bc)A(bc)^{-1} = bcAc^{-1}b^{-1} = bAb^{-1} = A;\\]\" width=\"307\" height=\"19\" />\nand if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/a/45a5ca10535cecc02a1922c94311dee8dc4e734d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$bAb^{-1} = A$\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/b/7fbaf3fd15773cca7efff0245e6fb1de7e129259.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = b^{-1}Ab$\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />.  Evidently, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/f/6cf4af8d788adeea37ed4595745e0026c20cdd05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\subseteq N(A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is a subgroup of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/a/86a7dc9448d1984863ede071f249a88b7cde960f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N(A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> is the largest subgroup of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Normal_subgroup\" title=\"Normal subgroup\">normal subgroup</a>.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Normalizer&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Normalizer&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Centralizer\" title=\"Centralizer\">Centralizer</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017212033\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.032 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 153/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 271/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4802/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.116      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.116      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6901:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017212033 and revision id 26004. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}